.TH BMELD 1 "2026-07-08" "tmeld" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bmeld \- Meld, in your browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bmeld
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIPATH\fR [\fIPATH\fR [\fIPATH\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bmeld
is
.BR tmeld (1)
served to a browser: the same vendored Meld engine, palette and keybindings,
rendered by CodeMirror with real SVG linkmap curves. It starts a local
server, prints a clickable URL, and exits with the same
.BR "git mergetool"
contract as tmeld \(em 0 only if the middle pane of a three-way merge was
saved.
.PP
\fBbmeld\fR and \fBtmeld \-\-web\fR are the same program. Every option that
says \fIwhat\fR to compare (paths, \fB\-\-diff\fR, \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-theme\fR,
\fB\-\-show\-line\-numbers\fR) behaves identically in both.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Listen on a fixed port instead of a random one. A fixed port plus a
\fBLocalForward\fR line in \fI~/.ssh/config\fR makes remote links open in your
local browser.
.TP
.BR \-\-bind " " \fIADDR\fR
Address to listen on. The default, 127.0.0.1, accepts connections from this
machine only. Binding wider (for example 0.0.0.0) makes the unguessable token
in the URL the only thing between the network and a process that reads and
writes the files under comparison, over cleartext HTTP; bmeld warns when you
do. Use it on a network you trust, or forward the port over SSH.
.TP
.BR \-\-advertise " " \fIHOST\fR
Hostname or address to put in the printed URL. Defaults to the bind address,
or this machine's outbound address when binding a wildcard.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not try to launch a local browser.
.TP
.BR \-\-grace " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for a browser to reconnect before treating the session as
abandoned. An abandoned merge exits 1.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. For a three-way merge, 0 only if the middle pane was saved.
1 if a merge was abandoned. 130 if interrupted (128 + SIGINT), so
\fBgit mergetool\fR treats a Ctrl\-C as a failure.
.SH NOTES
On Debian, bmeld needs \fBpython3\-aiohttp\fR, a Recommends of this package.
It is not bundled because it carries C extensions, which would make tmeld
architecture\-dependent.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmeld (1),
.BR meld (1)
